---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { AUTHOR, SITE } from '../consts';

const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    name: `About ${SITE.name}`,
    url: `${SITE.url}/about/`,
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#website` },
  },
];
---

<Base
  title={`About ${SITE.name} — who we are and why we exist`}
  description={`${SITE.name} is an independent prop firm research site — we buy evaluations, document payouts and track rule changes across the industry.`}
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="hub-head">
      <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>
    </header>
    <article class="article-body">
      <p>
        {SITE.name} exists because the prop firm industry has a trust problem. Between 2024 and
        2026, more than 80 prop firms shut down — many owing traders unpaid profits. Most "review"
        sites in this niche republish firm marketing copy in exchange for affiliate commissions and
        never mention the risks.
      </p>
      <p>We work differently:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>We buy every challenge we review.</strong> Ratings are based on purchased evaluations, not press kits.</li>
        <li><strong>We document payouts.</strong> A firm only earns a payout-reliability score after we (or verified community members) have requested and received real withdrawals.</li>
        <li><strong>We track rule changes monthly.</strong> Prop firm rules change constantly; every review shows its last-verified date.</li>
        <li><strong>Affiliate links never affect rankings.</strong> Our <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> is public, and firms cannot pay for placement.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Who writes {SITE.name}?</h2>
      <p>{AUTHOR.bio}</p>
      <p>
        Questions, corrections or payout-dispute reports: reach us via the
        <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Corrections are published with a changelog on the
        affected article.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
